Package: flycast
Architecture: amd64
# Flycast reaches Vulkan through vulkan.hpp's DYNAMIC dispatch loader: it vendors
# Vulkan-Headers and never links the loader, resolving libvulkan.so.1 with dlopen
# at startup instead. OpenGL is likewise resolved dynamically through SDL. Neither
# is visible to dh_shlibdeps, so both are listed by hand — without libvulkan1 the
# package installs cleanly and then fails to bring up a renderer.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 libvulkan1,
 libgl1
# The Vulkan ICD is what actually hands a device to the libvulkan1 loader; users
# on non-Mesa GPUs supply their own vendor driver, so this is a strong
# recommendation rather than a hard dependency.
Recommends: mesa-vulkan-drivers
Description: Sega Dreamcast, NAOMI and Atomiswave emulator
 Flycast is a multi-platform emulator for the Sega Dreamcast (1998) and for the
 Sega arcade boards that share its architecture — NAOMI, NAOMI 2 and Atomiswave.
 It emulates the console's SH-4 CPU with a dynamic recompiler and its PowerVR2
 graphics through either Vulkan or OpenGL, with per-pixel order-independent
 transparency for the effects the hardware rendered natively.
 .
 Disc images are read directly in GDI, CHD, CUE and CDI form. Save data is kept
 in emulated VMU files, and the emulator also supports widescreen and upscaled
 rendering, save states, network play, and RetroAchievements.
 .
 Flycast needs original console and arcade firmware to run. The Dreamcast BIOS
 (dc_boot.bin and dc_flash.bin) is recommended, and the NAOMI and Atomiswave
 BIOS files are required for those platforms. These are copyrighted Sega
 material and are NOT shipped with this package — you must supply them
 yourself, dumped from hardware you own, in ~/.local/share/flycast/data/.
 .
 This package ships the emulator as /usr/bin/flycast along with a desktop entry
 and hicolor icons, so it appears in the applications menu.
